{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>A trustworthy man.</b> [Meaning] any trustworthy man. Now it is superfluous, and it cannot be [read as] באמתו, for what would the verse come to teach? Moreover, [if so] he would not be in the image of a man at all."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "The word באמתו ('his truth/trustworthiness') would require reading the suffix as referring back to Og; Ibn Ezra rejects this on the grounds that it would imply no one could vouch for Og's human form."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:22:06.819352942Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}